Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:33:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-106: Esc gives up an edit in the grid; the row
 being edited marked, like WPF (0.106.0)

WPF's property grid: Esc while editing a value puts it back; the selected
property's row is marked. Here Esc did nothing (leaving the field wrote what was
typed) and nothing showed which row was being edited. Now Esc in a number field
(a run of Up / Down too), the Caption, Font.Name and a colour's value = back to
what it was when the editing started, nothing written; the row holding the focus
is marked (its background, its name bold).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (Width stepped twice then Esc, the Caption typed over then Esc: both back,
nothing sent; the focused row's background differs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
